==Trivia==
*The [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musket musket] is a muzzle-loaded long gun that appeared as a smoothbore weapon in the early 16th century, at first as a heavier variant of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arquebus arquebus], capable of penetrating [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plate_armour plate armour]. By the mid-16th century, this type of musket gradually disappeared as the use of heavy armour declined, but muskets continued as the generic term for smoothbore long guns until the mid-19th century. In turn, this style of musket was retired in the 19th century when [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rifled_musket rifles] became common.
*The Musketeer [[Cards|card]] could be a reference to the fourth Musketeer in the novel "''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Three_Musketeers The Three Musketeers]''", D'Artagnan, who was never considered to be in the group.
*The Musketeer is one of the first [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] cards to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Spear Goblins]], [[Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Prince]], and [[Balloon]].
*The Musketeer is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, Knight, Goblins, Bomber, Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Skeleton Army, Witch, P.E.K.K.A., Prince, Balloon, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Musketeer is 1 of 10 troops that have been featured under the [[Ruler Ability#Special Delivery|Special Delivery]] [[Ruler Ability|ruler ability]], the others being Knight, Skeleton Barrel, Mini P.E.K.K.A., Wizard, P.E.K.K.A., Giant Skeleton, [[Golem]], [[Sparky]], and Royal Ghost.
*The Musketeer is 1 of 23 cards that have had its [[Elixir]] cost changed, the others being Bomber, [[Fire Spirit]], Royal Recruits, [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], [[Three Musketeers]], [[Heal]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], Skeleton Army, P.E.K.K.A., Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], Bowler, [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Rage]], Fisherman, and the [[Monk]].
*The Musketeer wears a cape in her card image, but not in [[Basics of Battle|battle]].
*In the Arabic language setting of the game, the Musketeer is revealed to be a knight.
*The Musketeer, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Battle Healer]], Witch, Miner, Ice Wizard, and Bandit, is featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squaddies Squaddie] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The Musketeer, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, [[Ice Spirit]], Mini P.E.K.K.A., Giant, Wizard, Hog Rider, Witch, Prince, and Night Witch, is featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-theater-stickers/id1353823484 Clash Theater]. Also, along with the Archers, Goblins, Skeletons, Barbarians, Mini P.E.K.K.A., Wizard, Witch, Prince, and [[Princess]], she is also featured in the [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-a-rama/id1182384664 Clash-A-Rama] sticker pack.
*"Boomstick" may be a reference to the horror movie ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Army_of_Darkness Army of Darkness].''
*The Musketeer's deployment shares the same sound effects as the Hunter's attack load sound.
*The Musketeer is one of the first cards that the player unlocks, as a reward for the player winning the first Tutorial match through a Wooden Chest, alongside the Mini P.E.K.K.A..
**Unlike the Mini P.E.K.K.A., the player is not told to use the Musketeer during the tutorial.
*The Musketeer is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].
*In the [https://youtu.be/s67c93v1njk Star Level intro video], the Musketeer was shown to have 3 [[Star Points|Star Levels]]. However, she ended up with only 2 Star Levels in-game.
*Before the Musketeer's card release, the Musketeer's damage was decreased by 14%.

